o-send-data-centers-to-space-and-just-launched-a-satellite-to-test-whether-its-ambitious-plan-will-work-180989613/</link><description>这家科技巨头的目标是利用近地轨道上近乎恒定的阳光为数据中心供电。这颗实验卫星于 10 月 1 日发射，拥有四个计算机芯片，可以一次运行谷歌的 Gemini AI 15 分钟</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 20:01:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/google-wants-to-send-data-centers-to-space-and-just-launched-a-satellite-to-test-whether-its-ambitious-plan-will-work-180989613/</guid></item><item><title>数十件用人类头发编织而成的好奇艺术品来到纽约病态解剖图书馆</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/dozens-of-curious-artworks-created-with-woven-strands-of-human-hair-come-to-new-yorks-morbid-anatomy-library-180989577/</link><description>所谓的发饰在维多利亚时代流行起来，作为哀悼死者的一种方式</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/dozens-of-curious-artworks-created-with-woven-strands-of-human-hair-come-to-new-yorks-morbid-anatomy-library-180989577/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，这些野生狐猴的歌唱方式就像歌剧明星一样，在高音时张大嘴巴</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-wild-lemurs-sing-just-like-opera-stars-widening-their-mouths-as-they-hit-the-high-notes-study-suggests-180989603/</link><description>科学家怀疑这种音乐特征在人类和因德里斯身上独立出现，它们在大约 7400 万年前从共同祖先中分离出来。如今，在马达加斯加东部的茂密森林中，狐猴发出响亮而令人难以忘怀的叫声来相互交流</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 14:34:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-wild-lemurs-sing-just-like-opera-stars-widening-their-mouths-as-they-hit-the-high-notes-study-suggests-180989603/</guid></item><item><title>科学家在太平洋西北地区发现了两种新的海蜘蛛——它们看起来就像是直接从恐怖电影中走出来的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-discover-two-new-species-of-sea-spider-in-the-pacific-northwest-and-they-look-like-they-came-straight-out-of-a-horror-movie-180989598/</link><description>您无需担心小动物会追赶您，因为它们的直径只有几分之一英寸。它们与大约 1,400 种已知的海洋蜘蛛一样</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-discover-two-new-species-of-sea-spider-in-the-pacific-northwest-and-they-look-like-they-came-straight-out-of-a-horror-movie-180989598/</guid></item><item><title>涉嫌“毫无意义的破坏行为”摧毁了新安装的本杰明·哈里森雕像后，纵火调查正在进行中</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-arson-investigation-is-underway-after-a-suspected-sensless-act-of-vandalism-destroys-a-newly-installed-benjamin-harrison-statue-180989605/</link><description>这件 3D 打印作品由印第安纳大学印第安纳波利斯分校的学生和教师制作，并于 9 月 16 日安装</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 13:33:31 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-arson-investigation-is-underway-after-a-suspected-sensless-act-of-vandalism-destroys-a-newly-installed-benjamin-harrison-statue-180989605/</guid></item><item><title>新展览聚焦 4,500 年来破碎、爆炸和退化的艺术品，探索“碎片的力量”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-exhibition-spotlights-4500-years-of-broken-shot-up-and-degraded-artworks-to-explore-the-power-of-the-fragment-180989602/</link><description>该展览将在佛罗伦萨展出，并于明年在华盛顿举行，探讨了不同时期和不同文化中被毁坏雕塑的历史和影响</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-exhibition-spotlights-4500-years-of-broken-shot-up-and-degraded-artworks-to-explore-the-power-of-the-fragment-180989602/</guid></item><item><title>观看 2026 年尼康喜剧野生动物奖入围照片和视频中捕捉到的搞笑动物恶作剧</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-hilarious-animal-shenanigans-captured-in-photos-and-videos-shortlisted-for-the-2026-nikon-comedy-wildlife-awards-180989600/</link><description>从打喷嚏的驼鹿到现实生活中的愤怒的小鸟，今年的比赛收到了来自 112 个国家/地区的 10,000 多份参赛作品</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 23:01:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-hilarious-animal-shenanigans-captured-in-photos-and-videos-shortlisted-for-the-2026-nikon-comedy-wildlife-awards-180989600/</guid></item><item><title>阔别 1